{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head eb98be0f1ae1203d4cf63554fc2a9d7c4dfbad46 on builder/ar4-archive-unbound-20261117, all 11 artifacts, for request 0ceff627 under my promise 81cd038b. The implementation is AR-4 (request 4a73a509, promise 38a07fab, ruling 822d62f8 option A). The reporting artifact is the AR-4 note. The head's parent is main fc42cf3e.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole source diff.\n- `archive-host-item.ts`. The Directory branch now runs the register, claim, host, namespace, found-entry and seed checks before it reads the archive slot. A missing row stays `forbidden`. Only a row that passed every check and whose slot is not `journal` returns `ARCHIVE_UNBOUND`.\n- `archive-target.ts`. `one()` turns a refusal into `\"unbound\"` only when the answering scope is the Directory being checked (`same(at, directory)`). The branch read on the destination maps `\"unbound\"` to null. `resolve`, `resolveRoom`, `discover` and `discoverRoom` read `\"unbound\"` as null, and the new `bound()` returns it.\n- `apps/room/archive.ts`. The adapter repeats the same-Directory check and maps an `unbound` answer from any other scope to `forbidden`. It calls `target.bound()`.\n- `archive-driver.ts`. At the target step, `\"unbound\"` writes the marker through `rows.unbound()`, which replaces the pass's deferred retry, and ends the pass `disabled` with `next` one day out. A null clock falls back to the old retry.\n- `archive-row.ts`. The wake record reads `unbound` only as `\"directory\"` or `\"member\"`, with `pending` false, `stopped` false and a string `next`. Any other shape is unreadable. `unbound()` leaves a stopped writer alone. `signal()` returns early on a member marker. On a Directory marker it falls through and writes `next: at`, so a Directory commit wakes the Directory at once. `defer()` writes a record without `unbound`, so a later real failure replaces the marker with the AR-1 retry.\n- The seal moves in `security-entry-points.test.mjs` name AR-4 and match the five changed owners.\n\nWake rate (rule review-wake-rate-of-background-work):\n\n- What sets the next wake. `run()` sets no in-memory fallback for a `disabled` pass, so `wake()` returns the stored `next`, the daily recheck. When another owner's alarm runs the archive first, the wake check at `archive-driver.ts:215-217` reads the stored future `next` and ends the pass before any port call, as in AR-1.\n- The floor between passes. An unbound member waits one day (`ARCHIVE_UNBOUND_RECHECK_SECONDS = 86_400`), and its own commits leave the marker and the alarm alone. An unbound Directory waits one day, or until its next commit, whichever comes first.\n- What stops a reschedule loop. A due recheck makes one pass. That pass either writes the marker again (one more day) or meets a real failure and takes the AR-1 backoff (60 s floor, one-hour cap). No path writes a wake at or before now.\n- Requests per room per hour. grow-demo's four unbound scopes go from about 98 DO requests an hour (AR-3) to about 98 a day, about 4 an hour. Room A's lane goes from 1 pass an hour to 1 pass a day, and its per-minute commits add none. The test \"an unbound lane …\" measures this: 60 commits in an hour make 1 pass, and red 1 makes 61. The one remaining per-commit path is the Directory: each Directory commit makes at most one pass, which ends in a new marker. Directory commits are membership, install and binding acts, so that rate is low. The rate is bounded.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The reds in `artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-ar4-red`. Red 1 (a member commit re-arms the wake): \"no commit wakes an unbound member: expected 61 to be 1\". Red 2 (a Directory commit keeps the marker): the warm installed test fails 1 test, and the Directory still waits a day after `bind-archive`. Red 3 (an unreadable target counts as unbound): 7 tests fail, among them the AR-1 doubling from the floor.\n- The gate. END 32642801 passed at this head. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 11 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only fc42cf3e eb98be0f`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The driver can now tell \"no destination\" from a refusal, and the answer comes from the one scope that owns the slot. The marker lives in the existing wake record, so the AR-1 wake check stops other owners' alarms without new code. The cost of option A is the one the ruling accepted: after `bind-archive`, members archive at their next daily recheck.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. Only a peer object in the same namespace reaches `archiveItem`. The host answers `unbound` only to a caller that passed every check that would otherwise return the whole `repository` row, archive slot included, so the answer reveals nothing new. A scope other than the checked Directory cannot make a pass stop: the target and the room adapter both turn its `unbound` into a refusal. A malformed marker is unreadable and refuses the pass, and a stopped writer stays stopped.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The room adapter now calls only `bound()`. The tests still call `discover`, so it stays.\n\nFacts for the planner's deployment: the room Workers need a deployment and a DO rate read. At deployment, each unbound grow-demo scope makes one more failing pass when its current retry falls due, then stores the marker. Expect the :35 burst on dap-grow to stop within the hour after the deployment. The operator view does not show the marker.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25a73c91faccf21068b20cbd2d569f6688800e58","binding":"assigned","head":"eb98be0f1ae1203d4cf63554fc2a9d7c4dfbad46","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca98